[01:06.76] I have heard the echoes in the dark
[01:12.00] Dim and distant voices of the past
[01:20.58] And I've seen so far into the night
[01:28.26] And lingered in the land of no light
[01:35.22] Far beyond the
[01:38.56] Shrouded hours of dawn
[01:49.30] Through the mist
[02:19.14] Of daybreak I was borne
[02:24.22] But the day was
[02:29.68] Clouded still by night
[02:32.72] Leaving me in the land of no light
[02:38.68] Though I'd love to
[02:44.80] Say hello to you
[02:47.58] You might have to wait awhile
[02:51.20] To say goodbye
[02:54.70] For it must end as it began
[03:02.18] And then start again
[03:08.18] The day of darkness
[03:10.10] Comes to every man
[03:14.66] And lingers while he
[03:15.20] Reaches out his hand
[04:04.04] And he cannot know how it will end
[04:09.34] Till he finds out if he has a friend
[04:17.26] A friend ...
